BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Von Neumann Architecture of modern computing systems. Detail its primary structural components, functional registers, and the complete instruction execution cycle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Foundation:) Tj
T*
(   Proposed by mathematician John von Neumann in 1945, this architectural model established the) Tj
T*
(   stored-program computer concept,) Tj
T*
(   wherein program instructions and data share a common physical memory address space and are) Tj
T*
(   represented in unified binary format.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Primary Structural Subsystems:) Tj
T*
(   - Central Processing Unit \(CPU\):) Tj
T*
(   * Arithmetic Logic Unit \(ALU\): Executes elementary binary arithmetic \(addition, subtraction\)) Tj
T*
(   and logical bitwise operations \(AND, OR, XOR, shifts\).) Tj
T*
(   * Control Unit \(CU\): Decodes machine instructions, directs data flow across internal buses, and) Tj
T*
(   generates sequenced timing pulses.) Tj
T*
(   - Main Memory Unit \(RAM\): A linear array of byte-addressable memory cells storing active) Tj
T*
(   operating system code, application processes, and runtime data.) Tj
T*
(   - Input/Output \(I/O\) Subsystem: Interfaces the digital processing core with peripheral) Tj
T*
(   human-interface devices \(keyboards, monitors\) and secondary storage \(NVMe SSDs\).) Tj
T*
(   - System Bus Interconnect: Tripartite bus consisting of:) Tj
T*
(   * Data Bus \(bidirectional, width defines word size: 32/64 bits\).) Tj
T*
(   * Address Bus \(unidirectional from CPU to memory, width defines total physical addressability:) Tj
T*
(   2^n bytes\).) Tj
T*
(   * Control Bus \(transmits READ, WRITE, CLOCK, RESET, and INTERRUPT control signals\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Key Dedicated CPU Registers:) Tj
T*
(   - Program Counter \(PC\): Holds the memory address of the next sequential instruction to be) Tj
T*
(   fetched.) Tj
T*
(   - Memory Address Register \(MAR\): Holds the physical memory address currently being accessed on) Tj
T*
(   the address bus.) Tj
T*
(   - Memory Data Register \(MDR / MBR\): Holds the data word read from or to be written into the) Tj
T*
(   memory location specified by MAR.) Tj
T*
(   - Instruction Register \(IR\): Holds the binary instruction fetched from memory while its opcode) Tj
T*
(   is decoded by the Control Unit.) Tj
T*
(   - Accumulator \(AC\): Dedicated register holding intermediate arithmetic and logical results.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. The Four-Stage Instruction Execution Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1: Instruction Fetch \(IF\):) Tj
T*
(   MAR <- PC; MDR <- Memory[MAR]; IR <- MDR; PC <- PC + 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2: Instruction Decode \(ID\):) Tj
T*
(   Control unit decodes opcode in IR; determines required operands and addressing modes.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3: Execute \(EX\):) Tj
T*
(   ALU performs designated operation \(e.g., ADD, SUB, comparison\) on fetched register/memory) Tj
T*
(   operands.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 4: Memory Access / Write-Back \(WB\):) Tj
T*
(   Resultant computation is stored back into target destination register or main memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
