BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define Data Communication and state its five core structural components. Distinguish between Simplex, Half-Duplex, and Full-Duplex transmission modes with authentic computing examples.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Data Communication is the electronic exchange of digital or digitized information between two) Tj
T*
(   or more communicating entities via a physical transmission medium \(guided or wireless\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Five Fundamental Components:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Message: The information/data payload to be transmitted \(text, numeric data, digitized) Tj
T*
(   audio, compressed video, database records\).) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Sender \(Transmitter\): The source node that generates and dispatches the data message \(PC,) Tj
T*
(   smartphone, IoT sensor, workstation, IP video camera\).) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Receiver: The destination node intended to receive and process the message \(web server,) Tj
T*
(   printer, database host, client computer\).) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Transmission Medium: The physical transmission highway over which the signal propagates) Tj
T*
(   \(Twisted-pair copper cable, coaxial cable, single-mode fiber-optic cable, free-space radio) Tj
T*
(   waves\).) Tj
T*
(   - 5. Protocol: The formalized suite of rules, syntax, semantics, and synchronization) Tj
T*
(   conventions agreed upon by both communicating endpoints that governs data transfer.) Tj
T*
ET

