(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare the four fundamental physical Network Topologies: Mesh, Star, Bus, and Ring. Evaluate each with respect to: Link complexity, Cable length, Installation cost, Fault tolerance, and Failure impact.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mesh Topology \(Fully Connected\):) Tj
T*
(   - Link Complexity: For n nodes, requires n*\(n-1\)/2 dedicated physical links and \(n-1\) I/O ports) Tj
T*
(   per device.) Tj
T*
(   - Cable Length & Cost: Maximum possible cable length and highest installation/hardware cost.) Tj
T*
(   - Fault Tolerance: Exceptional redundancy; if one link fails, all other nodes communicate) Tj
T*
(   completely unaffected.) Tj
T*
(   - Failure Impact: Zero network-wide disruption. Ideal for core Internet ISP backbone routers) Tj
T*
(   and critical nuclear control systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Star Topology:) Tj
T*
(   - Link Complexity: Requires exactly n dedicated point-to-point links connected to a central) Tj
T*
(   multiport switch or hub.) Tj
T*
(   - Cable Length & Cost: Moderate cable length; significantly easier to install, configure, and) Tj
T*
(   troubleshoot than mesh.) Tj
T*
(   - Fault Tolerance: Failure of an individual link isolates only that specific connected) Tj
T*
(   workstation without impacting remaining network traffic.) Tj
T*
(   - Failure Impact: Single point of failure at the central switch \(if the central switch fails,) Tj
T*
(   the entire network collapses\). Standard topology for modern enterprise office LANs and homes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Bus Topology \(Linear Backbone\):) Tj
T*
(   - Link Complexity: One continuous shared backbone cable; devices connect via drop lines and BNC) Tj
T*
(   T-connectors. Terminators absorb reflections at ends.) Tj
T*
(   - Cable Length & Cost: Minimum cable consumption and lowest initial deployment cost.) Tj
T*
(   - Fault Tolerance: Very poor; difficult to isolate individual faults or cable breaks.) Tj
T*
(   - Failure Impact: Any break or impedance discontinuity in the main backbone cable reflects) Tj
T*
(   signals and disables the entire network. Obsolete in LANs, used in automotive CAN bus.) Tj
T*
ET

